            "isApproved": true,
            "id": "masked_c9cc4999-f063-4173-b4a2-67b2d68ad094",
            "numericRating": 5,
            "votes": null,
            "language": "en-gb",
            "rating": null,
            "content": "Great cabaret show! I would equate the show as more of a burlesque experience than dancing girls doing the can-can. The emcee was kinda cheeky but fun. There are no bad seats in the venue, a very intimate space. The champagne and canapés were just enough for a late evening snack. I didn’t find anything wrong with the sound system as mentioned in some posts from a few years ago. The male dancer who performed was very good at replicating many of the dance moves made famous by Michael Jackson and Channing Tatum. And the ladies of the show were superb(ah, to be that young and beautiful again!). Fun, cute, sultry, sexy would describe any of the numbers. I didn’t find their performances to be trashy or distasteful. They are artists and as such obviously work very hard at their craft of dance. They do lip sync to the music but it didn’t take away from the show. I found myself not focusing on the nudity at all but rather the creative lighting, choreography and talent. Check any puritanical inhibitions at the door and enjoy this celebration of beauty!",
            "user": {
